0067 - esp32s31: locking/spinlock.o in RAM text; memory cgroups on
===================================================================

Full copy of arch/riscv/kernel/vmlinux-xip.lds.S (includes 0053/0060-0062).
Makefile (committed in the repo) adds `--enable CGROUPS --enable MEMCG` and
`cgroup.memory=nokmem,nosocket` to the command line.

Adding CONFIG_MEMCG grew the image enough that the flash .spinlock.text's
relaxable call to do_raw_spin_lock (moved to RAM by the 0062 FASTFN list)
was shortened to a JAL during linker relaxation and then could not reach
its final RAM address: "relocation truncated to fit: R_RISCV_JAL against
do_raw_spin_lock". The object-wide fix is to put spinlock.o in
S31_FAST_OBJS, so both halves live in RAM text. That was tried on
2026-09-21 and did not boot (hart1 looping in handle_exception with sp
below _sdata) - which is exactly the early-exec failure patches/0061 later
fixed (RAM text non-executable before setup_vm_final). With 0061 in place
it boots (#386). _raw_spin_lock_irqsave now at c08576fa in RAM beside
do_raw_spin_lock; ~280 bytes of other __lockfunc code stay in flash.
